#### no-color-80
tidewater · Tidewater Studio license and updates

Usage  tidewater <command> [options]

License
  activate [key]            Add a license key (prompts; never an argument)
  status                    License, devices and offline time
  enroll                    Get the free license, when Tidewater Studio
                            offers one
  deactivate                Stop using your license on this device and free
                            its seat

Account
  login                     Sign in with your account in the browser
  logout                    Sign out on this device

Devices
  register                  Register this device without a license key
  devices list              List the devices using your license
  devices rename <deviceId> [label...]
                            Rename a device (no name clears it)
  devices deauthorize <deviceId>
                            Remove a device and free its seat

Settings
  config get <key>          Show one setting and where its value comes from
  config list               List the settings you can see
  config set <key> <value>  Change a setting on this device
  config reset <key>        Reset a setting to its default
  secret <key>              Print a secret delivered to this device
  mint <recipeId>           Get a short-lived token from a recipe

Updates
  update check              Check for a newer version
  update apply              Download and install the newer version
  changelog                 Show what's new in each version

Content
  packs status              Show installed and downloading content
  packs ensure <packIds...>
                            Download and install content, with progress

Support
  offline-request           Print the request code for offline activation
  import-bundle <file>      Activate from an offline activation file
  doctor                    Show what this device can do, for support
  completion <shell>        Print shell completion for bash, zsh or fish

Options
  --json                    JSON output for scripts, on every command
  --no-color                Plain text (also NO_COLOR=1)
  --ascii                   ASCII symbols only
  -h, --help                Help for a command

Run tidewater <command> --help for one command's options.

